      "guide_what_title": "Little programs that react to your pulse",
      "guide_what_text": "An addon can react to your heart rate, your zone and game moments, remember things, show notifications and draw in the overlay. For example: a warning when your pulse stays high, a glowing screen edge, or a count of your calmest boss fights.\n\nWrite it yourself (the guide with examples is on GitHub), start from an example, or let a coding assistant help. HypeRate Desktop itself contains no AI and sends nothing to AI services.",
      "guide_safe_title": "Safe by design",
      "guide_safe_text": "Every addon runs on its own in a sealed-off area. It cannot see your files, other apps or the rest of HypeRate, and gets only what you allow. Change anything in it, and you are asked again.\n\nAddons are off until you allow them. You can switch them off again any time in Settings.",
      "guide_wish_title": "1. Describe your wish",
      "guide_wish_text": "Click the + tile, give the addon a name and write in your own words what it should do. HypeRate creates a folder for it on this computer.",
      "guide_ai_title": "2. Build it: yourself or with help",
      "guide_ai_text": "The folder holds example code and a guide (AGENTS.md). Write the code yourself in any editor, or copy the ready-made task into a coding assistant such as Claude Code, Codex or Cursor; the guide explains to it how an addon works.",
      "guide_approve_title": "3. Check and switch on",
      "guide_approve_text": "When the addon is ready, open its tile in Integrations and switch it on. HypeRate shows you what it wants to use, such as your heart rate or a web address. Only allow what makes sense to you.",
      "guide_adjust_title": "4. Adjust and change",
      "guide_adjust_text": "Many addons have settings, such as a limit or a colour, that you change right on the addon's page. For anything bigger, edit the files yourself or create a new task under \"Change the addon\".",
      "guide_fix_title": "5. When something goes wrong",
      "guide_fix_text": "Errors show up on the addon's page. \"Copy as text\" gives you the error with hints, for you or your assistant. The log shows what the addon has been doing.\n\nYou can open this guide again any time with \"Help\".",
      "set_addons_desc": "Lets addons you made yourself run. Off stops all of them.",
